# /etc/paperbot/debate.env  (root:paperbot-debate 640: user paperbot cannot read it). Never commit the real file.
# The 24-hour debate room (docs/debate-room.md) is a PAID Anthropic API service and is OFF until you start it:
#   sudoedit /etc/paperbot/debate.env      then      sudo systemctl enable --now paperbot-debate
# Type or paste the key inside the editor only: never in the chat, never on a shell command line (history).
# Create the key in console.anthropic.com (Settings > API keys) and set a spend limit there too: that limit, not
# DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP, is the real stop. Keep it at or above DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP (the factory plan below: $70
# or more; the v4 start set $30, which stops the factory early). Only THIS service reads this file; the agent rooms
# (Claude Max) never do. install.sh never rewrites the server's /etc/paperbot/debate.env: a line added here later is
# missing there; change the line that is there, or add it at the end (sudoedit), then restart paperbot-debate.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Model (Haiku 4.5 is the cheap default; a pinned snapshot name). The owners' paper v4 choice (2026-10-05):
#   DEBATE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5   DEBATE_EVERY_MIN=30   DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP=30   DEBATE_EFFORT=low
# (docs/debate-room.md "Sonnet 5.5로 켜기": the dry run on a v4-shaped world gives about $17-22.5 a month before
# thinking, each 100 thinking tokens a round about $1.44 more; the code stops at 95% of the cap; console limit $30)
# Their 2026-10-06 choice for the idea factory (20 minutes stays, about $55-60 a month): see the factory block below
# (DEBATE_MODE=factory ... DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP=70, DEBATE_DAILY_USD_CAP=3); raise the console limit to $70 or more
# first. The model line below is the cheap default (Haiku): the factory's cost needs claude-sonnet-5-5 with
# DEBATE_EFFORT=low.
DEBATE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# One round (ONE API call with all the turns) every this many minutes. 20 = about $11-15 a month on Haiku;
# start with 60 on a small prepaid credit (docs/debate-room.md has the cost table).
DEBATE_EVERY_MIN=20
# Soft monthly cap in USD, counted from the API's own usage numbers: a warning at 80%, no more calls from 95%,
# never started when its worst case would pass the cap; resumes next month (KST) or after you raise it and run
# `sudo systemctl restart paperbot-debate`.
DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP=40
# Telegram warnings (the same bot and chat as agents.env: install.sh copies the two lines on a first install)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_CRITICAL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional (a commented line shows the default: removing its '#' changes nothing; to change a setting write
# NAME=VALUE without '#', alone on its line, with the value its comment gives). A bad value stops the service with an
# error (exit status 2).
# Prices in USD per million tokens. The built-in values (Haiku 4.5 $1 in / $5 out, Sonnet 5.5 $2 / $10, cache read
# 0.1x, cache write 1.25x for 5 minutes / 2x for 1 hour) only drive the cost counter and the cap: re-check them in
# the Anthropic console, and set these two when the model or the price differs (empty = the built-in price of the
# model in DEBATE_MODEL; Haiku's 1.0 / 5.0 here would make a Sonnet 5.5 month count half its real cost).
#DEBATE_PRICE_IN=
#DEBATE_PRICE_OUT=
# Safety guards: dollars in any 60 minutes (default cap / 24), per KST day (default off; the owners' factory plan:
# DEBATE_DAILY_USD_CAP=3)
#DEBATE_HOURLY_USD_CAP=
#DEBATE_DAILY_USD_CAP=
# Speaking turns per round (5-9, default 7: every seat once, then replies; an old 3 or 4 is read as 5), the answer's
# token ceiling, and the skip rule: a round is skipped (recorded, free) when fewer than this many trades closed since
# the last debate and there is no new alert or nightly check.
# The ceiling holds the thinking too (thinking + answer) and follows the turns: 7 turns 1,150, or 1,750 for a model
# that thinks (Sonnet 5.5 unless DEBATE_THINKING=between_tools); in factory mode +250 for the one lab idea (1,400 /
# 2,000). Leave DEBATE_MAX_TOKENS empty to get those; set by hand it must be 300-3000. The cap's worst case uses it.
#DEBATE_TURNS=7
#DEBATE_MAX_TOKENS=
#DEBATE_MIN_NEW_TRADES=10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The idea factory (owners' item B, docs/debate-room.md '아이디어 공장'). OFF unless DEBATE_MODE=factory: every round
# code picks ONE question about the 36 (the question bank), five specialist seats argue sides code assigns (차트 분석가,
# 리스크 책임자, 퀀트, 시장 분석가 split 찬성 / 반대 2-2, a new split every round; the 심판 last), and the 심판 writes ONE
# idea for the lab's real 5-year test. Code checks the idea, picks at most DEBATE_LAB_PER_DAY a day (09:00 and 21:00 KST
# for 2, 21:00 for 1) and the agents' lab intake queue tests it (deploy/agents.env AGENTS_LAB_INTAKE_DEBATE_PER_DAY must
# be the same number or more). Rollback with no code change: DEBATE_MODE=classic (or empty), then restart.
# The owners' choice (2026-10-06): 20 minutes stays, Sonnet 5.5 effort low, about $55-60 a month with the deep debate:
#   DEBATE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5   DEBATE_EFFORT=low   DEBATE_EVERY_MIN=20
#   DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP=70   DEBATE_DAILY_USD_CAP=3
#   DEBATE_MODE=factory   DEBATE_LAB_PER_DAY=2   DEBATE_DEEP=1
# (`once --dry-run` with those lines prints the system prompt's size, every question kind's request, the deep debate
# and the month: on the v4-shaped test data about $0.019 a round, $0.023 with 400 thinking tokens, about $50 a month for
# 2,160 rounds, plus about $3.5 for the deep debate; skipped rounds cost nothing. The code stops at 95% of the monthly
# cap and never starts a call whose worst case would pass the month, the day or the hour guard.)
# classic (or empty) = the default debate; the idea factory needs DEBATE_MODE=factory written out
#DEBATE_MODE=classic
#DEBATE_LAB_PER_DAY=2
# The daily deep debate (factory mode only): once a KST day from DEBATE_DEEP_AT, claude-opus-5-5 in THREE separate calls
# (주장 by the two 찬성 seats -> 반박 by the two 반대 seats, reading part 1 -> 심판, reading both, writes the idea), on the
# day's most important question; its own month line inside DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP (it stops there, the regular rounds
# go on). 4,000 tokens a call at most (thinking included: Opus 5.5 always thinks, effort sets how much). On: DEBATE_DEEP=1
#DEBATE_DEEP=0
#DEBATE_DEEP_AT=20:00
#DEBATE_DEEP_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
#DEBATE_DEEP_EFFORT=low
#DEBATE_DEEP_MAX_TOKENS=4000
#DEBATE_DEEP_MONTHLY_USD_CAP=10
# Opus 5.5 is built in at $4 in / $20 out per million (cache reads 0.05x); set these when the console says otherwise
#DEBATE_DEEP_PRICE_IN=
#DEBATE_DEEP_PRICE_OUT=
# Sonnet 5.5 thinks by default (adaptive) and its thinking tokens are billed as OUTPUT tokens: they are in the API's
# usage.output_tokens, so the cost counter and the monthly cap count them. DEBATE_EFFORT=low (sent as
# output_config.effort) keeps the thinking short; Sonnet 5.5's own default is high. To turn thinking off on Sonnet 5.5
# use DEBATE_THINKING=between_tools; "disabled" is refused by Sonnet 5.5 (the service stops at start with exit 2).
# Haiku 4.5 takes neither setting: leave both empty there. The owners' plan (claude-sonnet-5-5): DEBATE_EFFORT=low.
#DEBATE_THINKING=
#DEBATE_EFFORT=
